  "question": {
    "text": "If the equation of the locus of a point equidistant from the point $\\left(a_1, b_1\\right)$ and $\\left(a_2, b_2\\right)$ is $\\left(a_1-b_2\\right) x+\\left(a_1-b_2\\right) y+c=0$, then the value of 'c' is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{\\mathrm{a}_1^2+\\mathrm{b}_1^2-\\mathrm{a}_2^2-\\mathrm{b}_2^2}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} a_2^2+b_2^2-a_1^2-b_1^2$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{a}_1^2-\\mathrm{a}_2^2+\\mathrm{b}_1^2-\\mathrm{b}_2^2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a_1^2+a_2^2+b_1^2+b_2^2\\right)$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left(h-a_1\\right)^2+\\left(k-b_1\\right)^2=\\left(h-a_2\\right)^2+\\left(k-b_2\\right)^2$\n$\\left(a_1-a_2\\right) x+\\left(b_1-b_2\\right) y+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a_2^2+b_2^2-a_1^2-b_1^2\\right)=0$\n$C=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(a_2^2+b_2^2-a_1^2-b_1^2\\right)$"
  }
